Later in the afternoon, I walk over to Jonas.
He is sitting at his place and working on his laptop.
"Do you have a moment?" I ask him.
Jonas nods and looks at me.
"I am visiting Nele on Friday," I say.
"She is making a big dinner."
"Do you know what I can bring?"
Jonas thinks for a moment.
"I know that Nele loves sweet things," he says.
"A nice dessert is surely a great idea."
"So I give her a nice dessert?" I ask.
"Exactly, or a small tart," Jonas answers.
"I am sure that she will be happy about that," he adds.
"That is a very good tip," I say, smiling.
"I will look for a good bakery later."
